# Trivy ignore file — scoped to the moor/copilot image ONLY.
#
# Wired into CI via the `trivy scan copilot` step's `trivyignores:` input
# (.github/workflows/ci.yml). Every other moor image is scanned with NO
# ignore file: base/node/rust/python/egress stay on the strict
# fixable-HIGH/CRITICAL gate. This file exists solely because Copilot's
# agent is distributed as a ~174MB compiled binary
# (@github/copilot-<platform>) that vendors its own npm dependencies
# INSIDE the binary. Those versions cannot be bumped with an npm
# override, dedupe, or a Dockerfile change — only a newer upstream
# @github/copilot release can move them. See images/copilot/Dockerfile.
#
# Each entry below is a specific CVE, not a blanket suppression. All
# three are Denial-of-Service (not RCE, not data exfiltration), against
# an agent process that runs inside moor's strongest containment:
# non-root, read-only rootfs, cap_drop ALL, default-deny egress. The
# practical exposure of DoS'ing an agent inside a throwaway sandbox is
# low. Re-check and remove any entry once @github/copilot ships a release
# whose bundled binary carries the fixed version.
#
# Verified against @github/copilot 1.0.89 (the latest stable at the time
# of writing); revisit when the pinned/installed version changes.

# brace-expansion 5.0.9 — DoS via stack exhaustion from crafted brace
# patterns. Fixed upstream in 5.0.10; bundled unpatched in the copilot
# binary. Re-check on the next @github/copilot bump.
CVE-2026-102276

# brace-expansion 5.0.9 — DoS via uncontrolled recursion in nested brace
# patterns. Fixed upstream in 5.0.11; bundled unpatched. Re-check on bump.
CVE-2026-102278

# undici 6.28.0 — DoS via unrequested WebSocket subprotocol. Fixed
# upstream in 6.28.1; bundled unpatched. Re-check on bump.
CVE-2026-19534
